[size=5][b][color=#f2dc4b]EDGERUNNERS MOD MANAGER[/color][/b][/size]
[i]A new way to manage Cyberpunk 2077 mods: every mod, profile and log in one app.[/i]

[url=https://skyehosting.github.io/edgerunners-mod-manager/]Project page[/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/skyehosting/edgerunners-mod-manager]Source code[/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/skyehosting/edgerunners-mod-manager/releases]All releases[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://skyehosting.github.io/edgerunners-mod-manager/assets/nexus/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=4][b][color=#f2dc4b]What it is[/color][/b][/size]
Modding Cyberpunk usually means a browser, a downloader, a load order tool, a log viewer and a lot of guessing. Edgerunners Mod Manager puts all of it in one app, built for Cyberpunk 2077 alone. It downloads from Nexus, keeps a separate setup for every playthrough, sorts the load order, reads every mod's logs as you play, and points at the mod behind a crash.

[size=4][b][color=#f2dc4b]Main features[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Mods[/b] - every mod with its status, conflicts, updates and version. Turn mods on and off, update and repair them, and choose which mod wins each file conflict.
[*][b]Browse Nexus and Downloads[/b] - search Nexus inside the app, pick a mod's files, and the mods it needs come along. Free and Premium accounts both work.
[*][b]Profiles[/b] - a separate set of mods and load order for every playthrough. Switch from the sidebar in one click, or share a profile with a friend as a code.
[*][b]Load order[/b] - drag archives, type a new position, or let Auto-sort put add-ons above what they need.
[*][b]Game log[/b] - CET, RED4ext, redscript, ArchiveXL, TweakXL and more in one live timeline. Every play is kept and filed under its profile, with crashes traced to a mod.
[*][b]Config editor[/b] - edit mods' settings files in a built-in editor with colours for each format. The original is kept, so it can always be put back.
[*][b]AI Assistant (optional)[/b] - your own AI provider, or a model running on your PC, reads your mods and logs and explains errors in plain words. It changes nothing without your OK.
[*][b]Already using another mod manager?[/b] Bring its mods and game profiles over in a click, with no extra disk space (Vortex and Mod Organizer 2).
[*][b]Play[/b] - starts the game, and deploys REDmods first when they changed.
[*][b]Seven themes[/b] and a custom theme editor, a short setup wizard the first time, and the app updates itself.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#f2dc4b]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the installer from the [b]Files[/b] tab.
[*]Run it. It installs for your Windows user only, with no admin rights. The installer is not code-signed yet, so Windows may show "Windows protected your PC": choose [b]More info[/b], then [b]Run anyway[/b].
[*]Follow the short welcome. It finds your game and connects your Nexus account with your personal API key (nexusmods.com, then your account's API Keys page). Every step can be skipped.
[/list]
[b]This is an app, not a mod:[/b] don't install it through Vortex or another mod manager.

[size=4][b][color=#f2dc4b]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 (Steam, GOG, Epic or the Xbox app; the game folder is found automatically)
[*]A Nexus Mods account and its personal API key. Premium downloads directly; a free account clicks "Slow download" once per file, and the app does the rest.
[*]Optional, for the AI Assistant: an AI provider (OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, or a local model such as Ollama or LM Studio)
[/list]
7-Zip comes with the app. There is nothing else to install.

[size=4][b][color=#f2dc4b]Good to know[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Updates:[/b] the app updates itself. It downloads new versions in the background and installs them with a short notice (Settings can make it ask first).
[*][b]Your keys stay yours:[/b] your Nexus and AI keys are encrypted on your PC and only ever sent to Nexus and to the AI provider you choose.
[*][b]Uninstalling:[/b] first turn off the mods this app manages (Mods page: select them, then Disable), so the game folder is left clean. Then remove the app in Windows Settings, Apps.
[*][b]Found a bug?[/b] Post it in the Bugs tab or on [url=https://github.com/skyehosting/edgerunners-mod-manager/issues]GitHub[/url]. Game log, Export report collects what is needed to look into it (never your keys).
[/list]

